><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: Although breast protective equipment was worn by only 17% offemale contact football players, most players who used it per-ceived it to be effective.•Female contact football players reported they did not use breastprotective equipment because they did not know it existed, it wasuncomfortable to wear or fitted poorly.•One in three players perceived that their sports bra providedsome protection against contact breast injuries; however, morethan half of the players wore ill-fitted bras, which might compromise the support and protection of these garments. Greatereducation on breast support and bra fit is required.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
